    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 passing).\n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented for the soft-delete of owners:\n\n**Soft-delete on DELETE** (`DeleteOwner.java`): instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `deleted = true` and saves, so the row is retained and the endpoint still returns 2xx.\n\n**New `deleted` field**:\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` column (defaulting to `false`) with getter/setter, so a newly created owner is `false`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` surfaces it (generates `getDeleted`/`setDeleted` on `OwnerDto`, auto-mapped by MapStruct).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 ignore `deleted` when mapping the request `OwnerFieldsDto` \u2192 `Owner` (it's server-owned).\n- DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` column.\n\n**Duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners**:\n- `EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` \u2014 skips existing owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking household/exact-identity match no longer causes a 409 when the only match was soft-deleted.\n- `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 likewise skips deleted owners for the soft-duplicate flag.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass:\n- `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` \u2014 create \u2192 `deleted:false`, delete \u2192 2xx, GET still returns owner with `deleted:true`.\n- `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` \u2014 re-creating a soft-deleted owner's identical payload is allowed.",
